{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/41496-break-to-heal-success-goal","id":41496,"title":"Break to Heal Success Goal?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-02T20:55:58-08:00","id":41496,"title":"Break to Heal Success Goal?","content":"I'm confused about the &quot;Break to Heal&quot; exploit. How many success do you need? Is it just a goal of one or do you need enough to pass the durability of the object and deal enough structure damage to break it all in one instant action?<br /> <br /> That could be difficult for anything that has a Structure of 3 or more which could add up to 5 successes depending on the durability. Then what confuses me even more is that the Fail says &quot;The demon fails to heal the target, though the object is still broken.&quot; Well, if you didn't roll enough successes to break the object, then how is it &quot;still broken.&quot;<br /> <br /> Structure rating has to be considered, because on the pass you can &quot;heal all bashing&quot; or &quot;change all aggravated to lethal&quot; or &quot;heal lethal equal to the structure rating of the object.&quot; So you heal all bashing or change all aggravated to lethal by smashing any tiny easily broken thing, but to heal lethal you need to take a risk of trying to break something big? That just doesn't seem right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1891-mdfs","name":"MDFS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T20:35:36-08:00","id":42127,"title":"","content":"After some thought, a friend of mine suggested: Because its a supernatural break attempt it should bypass duration. This way the structure of the object is the number of successes needed. Therefore, if a player needs to heal several points of lethal damage they would need to risk trying to break something with a higher structure. The player only gets one attempt, as the supernatural energies break the object regardless. This way you won't have a player needing to roll a large number of successes due to durability, but it forces the player to make a risk-reward judgement. <br /> <br /> Any small object broken would heal bashing, because bashing isn't serious. However, we haven't come up with a good balance for success goal for aggravated damage. Anyone have any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1891-mdfs","name":"MDFS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}